card.statement:
Let $(A,L,\alpha)$ be a Lie-Rinehart monoid in $\calC$. Suppose $(\mathfrak{L}, \mathfrak{u})$ is a Lie monoid in $\calC$, and $\mathcal{H}: L \rightarrow \mathfrak{L}\otimes A$ a crossed homomorphism. Then the category ${\bf WMod}^{\calC}_A{\big(L\big)}$ is a strict left module category over the monoidal category $\mathrm{ \bf Mod}_{\calC}(\mathfrak{L})$. Specifically, for all $(V,\psi), (V', \psi')\in $ $\mathrm{ \bf Mod}_{\calC}(\mathfrak{L})$, and $(M;\rho, \gamma), (M'; \rho',\gamma') \in$ ${\bf WMod}^{\calC}_A{\big(L\big)}$, we have a bifunctor

\begin{align*}
\mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{H}}: \mathrm{ \bf Mod}_{\calC}(\mathfrak{L}) \times {\bf WMod}^{\calC}_A{\big(L\big)} &\rightarrow {\bf WMod}^{\calC}_A{\big(L\big)} \\
((V,\psi), (M; \rho,\gamma) ) & \mapsto (V\otimes M; \psi \vartriangleright \rho, \psi \vartriangleright \gamma ).
\end{align*}

On morphisms, it is defined by $\mathcal{F}_{\mathcal{H}}(\varphi, \phi)=\varphi\otimes \phi$, where $\varphi:V\to V'$ is a homomorphism of $\mathfrak{L}$-modules and $\phi:M\to M'$ is a homomorphism of weak modules over $(A,L,\alpha)$.
